<DocsLayout
  title="Uninstall"
  description="Clean removal. Vault data is preserved by default."
  current="uninstall"
>
  <p>From your cloned repo:</p>

  <pre><code>bash scripts/thinkos-uninstall.sh --dry-run    # see the plan
bash scripts/thinkos-uninstall.sh              # apply it</code></pre>

  <p>
    The uninstaller reads <code>~/.thinkos/install-manifest.json</code> —
    written when you installed — and undoes exactly what was installed.
    If the manifest is missing (old installs from before manifest-writing),
    it falls back to repo enumeration.
  </p>

  <h2>Flags</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>--dry-run</code> — print the plan; don't touch anything.</li>
    <li><code>--keep-vault</code> (default) — your vault folder stays on disk.</li>
    <li><code>--remove-vault</code> — also delete the vault directory.</li>
    <li><code>--keep-mcps</code> (default) — leave bundle MCPs (Slack, Gmail, etc.) registered.</li>
    <li><code>--remove-mcps</code> — also unregister bundle MCPs.</li>
    <li><code>--keep-basic-memory</code> (default) — leave Basic Memory installed.</li>
    <li><code>--remove-basic-memory</code> — also unregister the BM project and offer to uninstall the binary.</li>
    <li><code>--all</code> — equivalent to <code>--remove-vault --remove-mcps --remove-basic-memory</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Backups</h2>
  <p>
    If <code>~/.claude/CLAUDE.md</code> or <code>~/.claude/commands/</code> had
    content before Think OS was installed, the original is backed up to
    <code>~/.claude/CLAUDE.md.pre-thinkos-backup-&lt;date&gt;</code> and
    <code>~/.claude/commands.pre-thinkos-backup-&lt;date&gt;/</code>.
    Those backups stay in place after uninstall — remove them yourself if
    you're sure you don't need them.
  </p>

  <h2>What you'll need to do manually</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If you installed plugins via a bundle, run <code>/plugin remove &lt;slug&gt;@&lt;marketplace&gt;</code> in Claude Code for each one — there's no CLI for plugin removal.</li>
    <li>If you set up scheduled triggers, list them with <code>/thinkos-automate list</code> before uninstalling and remove each with <code>/thinkos-automate remove &lt;name&gt;</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="text-muted text-sm mt-12">
    Rendered docs coming soon. For now, the source files in the repo are authoritative.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
